#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Keyboard Input Switcher for LG, Linux version (made for Bazzite; plain Python 3, no extra packages).
#
# Switches an LG monitor's input with LG's non-standard DDC command: VCP 0xF4 sent with source
# address 0x50 (standard DDC/CI uses 0x51, which LG ignores for input select). On Linux the command
# goes through the kernel's /dev/i2c-* devices, so it works with any graphics driver that exposes
# the monitor's DDC bus (NVIDIA, AMD and Intel all do).
#
#   lg-input-switcher hdmi1        switch now (also: dp1, hdmi2, ...)
#   lg-input-switcher daemon       watch the keyboard for the shortcuts (what "install" sets up)
#   lg-input-switcher install      copy to ~/.local/bin and start the shortcut service at login
#   lg-input-switcher doctor       check what's missing
#
# Unofficial. Not made by, affiliated with, or endorsed by LG Electronics. Public domain (Unlicense).

